hadiths[361]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7201","(7196): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra’il narrated to us, Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Shu’bah informed us, Asim ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah mentioning from his father that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant who sends a prayer upon me but the angels send prayers upon him as long as he sends prayers upon me; so let a servant do little of that or much."
"7202","(7197): Ishaq narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, that a man of Banu Fazarah married a woman for two sandals, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted her marriage."
"7203","(7198): Ishaq narrated to us, Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He says, meaning the Lord, Mighty and Majestic: The womb is a derivative from Me; whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him."
"7204","(7199): Ishaq narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, saying: al-Mas’udi narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send us out with no food but an advance of dates; we divided it handful by handful, ending with date by date. By Allah, since we lost them we have felt their loss."
"7205","(7200): Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Amir ibn Rabi’ah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the funeral procession, stand for it until it passes you by or is laid down."
"7206","(7201): Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Asim ibn Ubayd Allah informed me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you after me who pray the prayer delaying it. If they pray it in its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them; if they pray it outside its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and against them. Whoever separates from the community has shed Islam, and whoever dies having broken the covenant meets Allah with no proof for him. I said: Who informed you of this? He said: Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7207","(7202): Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father informed us, I heard al-Nu’man ibn Rashid narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gesturing with his head wherever his face turned."
"7208","(7203): Abu al-Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you who pray the prayer in its time and delay it past its time. What they pray in its time and you pray with them, is for you and for them; what they delay past its time and you pray with them, is for you and against them. Whoever separates from the community has removed the yoke of Islam from his neck, and whoever dies breaking the covenant comes on the Day of Resurrection with no proof for him."
"7209","(7204): Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Ishaq said: Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Amr, the freedman of the family of Manzur ibn Sayyar, narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Amir ibn Rabi’ah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was circumambulating the House when his sandal strap broke; a man brought out a strap from his sandal and went to fasten it on the sandal of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he pulled it away and said: This is preferring, and I do not like preferring."
"7210","Report of Abu Basrah al-Ghifari (7205): Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Ya’qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa’d narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Khayr ibn Nu’aym al-Hadrami, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayrah al-Saba’i, and he was trustworthy, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Abu Basrah al-Ghifari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Asr prayer; when he finished his prayer, Ya’qub once said: when he turned from his prayer, he said: This prayer was offered to those before you but they were negligent of it and abandoned it. Whoever of you prays it, his reward is doubled twofold, and there is no prayer after it until the witness is seen, and the witness is the star."
"7211","(7206): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra’il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Munib al-Adani narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from a man of Tayyi’, and he praised him well, who said: I used to ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to show me the Name by which, when He is called by it, He answers. Then I saw written in the stars in the sky: O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"7212","(7207): al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za’idah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi’, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, who said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered his house, he recited Ayat al-Kursi in the corners of his house."
"7213","(7208): Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Yahya, from Mujahid, who said: A man passed by Ibn Abbas and said: This man loves me. They said: How do you know, O Abu Abbas? He said: Because I love him."
"7214","Report of Zayd ibn Harithah (7209): Sa’id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Kathir, from Ali ibn Abd Allah, from Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of the dawn prayer, so he said: Pray it with me today and tomorrow. When he was at the valley of Namirah at al-Juhfah, he prayed it when dawn rose; then when he was at Dhu Tuwa he delayed it, until people said: Has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) been taken? They said: If only we had prayed? Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed it before the sun, then turned to the people and said: What did you say? They said: We said: If only we had prayed? He said: If you had done so, punishment would have befallen you. Then he called the questioner and said: The prayer is between these two prayers."
"7215","(7210): Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih Abu Muhammad al-Azdi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from his father, from al-Bara’, from Zayd ibn Harithah, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, you made brotherhood between me and Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"7216","(7211): Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from al-Bara’ ibn Azib, that Zayd ibn Harithah said: O Messenger of Allah, you made brotherhood between me and Hamzah."
"7217","(7212): Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, dictating to us from his book, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah and Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib ibn Abi Balta’ah, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Harithah, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a hot day of the days of Makkah, with him having me behind him, to one of the idols, and we had slaughtered a sheep for him and cooked it. He said: Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl met him, and each greeted the other with the greeting of the pre-Islamic era. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Zayd, why do I see your people have hated you? He said: By Allah, O Muhammad, that is without any offense of mine toward them, but I went out seeking this religion until I came to the rabbis of Fadak, and found them worshipping Allah and associating with Him. I said: This is not the religion I seek. So I went out until I came to the rabbis of Syria and found them worshipping Allah and associating with Him. I said: This is not the religion I seek. Then an old man of them said: You ask about a religion which we know no one worships Allah by except an old man at al-Hirah. So I went out until I came to him; when he saw me he said: From where are you? I said: From the people of the House of Allah, from the people of thorns and the west. He said: The religion you seek has appeared in your land; a prophet has been sent, his star has risen, and all those you saw are in error. I have felt nothing yet, O Muhammad. He said: And he brought the meal near to him. He said: What is this, O Muhammad? He said: A sheep we slaughtered for one of the idols. He said: I would never eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned. Zayd ibn Harithah said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the House. We separated and he circumambulated it, I with him, and al-Safa and al-Marwah. At al-Safa and al-Marwah were two idols of copper: one called Isaf and the other called Na’ilah, and when the polytheists circumambulated they wiped over them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wipe them, for they are filth. I said to myself: I shall surely touch them to see what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says. So I touched them, and he said: O Zayd, were you not forbidden? Zayd ibn Amr died, and revelation was sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Zayd: He will be raised as a nation alone."
"7218","Report of Khabbab ibn al-Aratt (7213): Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Isma’il, from Qays, from Khabbab, who said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Ka’bah, and said: Will you not seek victory for us? He sat up with his face reddened and said: Among those before you a man would be taken, a pit dug for him in the ground, then a saw brought and placed over his head, yet that did not turn him from his religion; or he would be combed with iron combs beneath his flesh of bone and sinew, yet that did not turn him from his religion. Allah will surely complete this matter until a rider travels from San’a to Hadramawt fearing none but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and the wolf for his sheep. But you are hasty."
"7219","(7214): Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Yahya ibn Ja’dah, who said: Some Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Khabbab and said: Rejoice, O Abu Abd Allah, you will meet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Basin. He said: What about this, pointing to the top of the house and its bottom, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices one of you of this world like the provision of a rider."
"7220","(7215): Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma’il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a man of Abd al-Qays who had been with the Khawarij then left them, who said: They entered a village, and Abd Allah ibn Khabbab came out frightened dragging his cloak. They said: You need not fear. He said: By Allah, you have frightened me. They said: You need not fear. He said: By Allah, you have frightened me. They said: Are you Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. They said: Did you hear from your father a hadith narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he mentioned tribulation: the one sitting in it is better than the standing, the standing better than the walking, and the walking better than the hastening? He said: If that reaches you, be the slain servant of Allah. Ayyub said: And I know he only said: And do not be the killing servant of Allah. They said: Did you hear this from your father narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. So they brought him forward at the bank of the river and struck his neck; his blood flowed as if a sandal strap pouring out, and they ripped open his slave-woman’s belly over what was in it."
"7221","Continuation of the report of Zayd ibn Arqam (7216): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra’il narrated to us, Mu’tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Dawud al-Tufawi narrating from Abu Muslim al-Bajali, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at the end of prayer: O Allah, our Lord and Lord of everything, I am a witness that all servants are brothers; O Allah, our Lord and Lord of everything, make me devoted to You and my family in every hour of this world and the Hereafter, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor; hear and answer; Allah is Greatest, the Greatest, Light of the heavens and the earth; Allah is Greatest, the Greatest; Allah suffices me and He is the bestGuardian; Allah is Greatest, the Greatest."
"7222","(7217): Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Dawud al-Basri, from Abu Muslim al-Bajali, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he supplicated at the end of prayer, saying: Then he mentioned the like of it or its equivalent."
"7223","(7218): Ishaq ibn Abi Isra’il narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Sa’id informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended, so when one of you wishes to enter the lavatory, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from male and female devils."
"7224","(7219): Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies, then he mentioned its equivalent."
"7225","(7220): Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: Cloaks came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he divided them among his Companions. My father Makhramah said to me: Let us go to him; perhaps he will give us something of them. My father came to the door and said: He is here. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his voice and came out with a cloak. It is as if I look at him showing my father the beauties of the cloak, saying: I had hidden this for you. Abu Muhammad Salih said: I said to my father: Why did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do this with Makhramah? He said: He used to guard against his tongue."
"7226","(7221): Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Isma’il ibn Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the sermon of need, saying: All praise belongs to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of ourselves and the evils of our deeds; whom Allah guides none misguides, and whom He misguides none guides; and I bear witness there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and I bear witness Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Abu Ubaydah said: And I heard from Abu Musa saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If you wish to join your sermon with verses of the Qur’an, say: Fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims; and fear Allah through whom you ask one another and the wombs, indeed Allah is ever over you an Observer; fear Allah and speak upright words, He will amend your deeds and forgive your sins, and whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has attained a great triumph. Then as for what follows, speak your need."
"7227","(7222): Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abd Allah ibn Nu’aym, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Arzab al-Ash’ari, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Abu Amir al-Ash’ari over the pursuit cavalry on the day of Hunayn. When Hawazin fled, he pursued them until he caught Durayd ibn al-Simmah, whose breath quickened, and Ibn Durayd killed Abu Amir. Abu Musa said: I attacked Ibn Durayd and killed him, took the banner, and returned with the people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he saw the banner in my hand he said: O Abu Musa, has Abu Amir been killed? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He raised his hands supplicating for him, saying: O Allah, place Abu Amir among the most numerous on the Day of Resurrection, this or its like."
"7228","(7223): Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, al-Rabi’ ibn Badr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two and more are a congregation."
"7229","(7224): al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Sa’id narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, that Abu Musa led them in prayer; when they sat at the end of their prayer, a man of the people said: Has the prayer been established with righteousness and zakat? When Abu Musa turned he faced the people and said: Which of you said such and such words? The people fell silent twice. He said: Perhaps you, O Hittan, said it? He said: I did not say it, and I feared you would blame me for it. Then a man of the people said: I said it, and I intended only good thereby. Abu Musa said: Do you not know what you say in your prayer? The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, explained our Sunnah, and taught us our prayer, saying: When you pray, straighten your rows, then let one of you lead you. When the imam says takbir, say takbir; when he says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, say: Amin, Allah will answer you. When he says takbir and bows, say takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that. When he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, Allah will hear for you, for Allah said upon the tongue of His Prophet: Allah hears whoever praises Him. When he says takbir and prostrates, say takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is for that. Until when at the sitting, let the first of one’s speech be: Greetings, prayers, good words belong to Allah; peace upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Seven phrases of the greeting of prayer. Sa’id said: I do not know whether that was in Abu Musa’s words, or something Qatadah used to say, meaning by his words: seven phrases."
"7230","(7225): Jubarah ibn Mughallis al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt."
"7231","(7226): Jubarah narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make the end of my nation in stabbing and plague. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we know stabbing, but what is plague? He said: The pricks of your enemies from the jinn, and in it is martyrdom."
"7232","(7227): Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Isra’il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"7233","(7228): Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Qarazah ibn Hassan, who said: I heard Abu Musa on a Friday on the minbar of Basra saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Hour while I was present, and said: None knows it but Allah, none manifests it in its time but He; but I shall tell you of its conditions and what precedes it: before it is a dam of tribulations and harj. It was said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It is in the tongue of Abyssinia: killing; and that people’s hearts become light, mutual estrangement is cast among them so hardly anyone knows anyone, people of understanding are taken away, and a dregs of people remain who know no good nor deny evil."
"7234","(7229): Bundar narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, who heard Abu Burdah, who heard Abu Musa, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man wishes to marry off his daughter, let him seek her permission."
"7235","(7230): Bundar narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"7236","(7231): Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Isma’il narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets passed by the rock of al-Rawha’, among them Musa, the Prophet of Allah, barefoot wearing cloaks, heading to the Ancient House of Allah."
"7237","(7232): Sa’id ibn Yahya ibn Sa’id al-Umawi narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa narrated to me, from his father, who said: We went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by sea until we came to Makkah, my brothers with me: Abu Amir ibn Qays, Abu Ruhm ibn Qays, and Muhammad ibn Qays, fifty of the Ash’aris and six of Akk; then we migrated by sea until we reached Madinah. (7233): Abu Burdah said: Abu Musa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: People have one migration, but you have two migrations."
"7238","(7234): Sa’id ibn Yahya ibn Sa’id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Burdah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour is harj. We said: What is harj? He said: Killing, killing, until a man kills his neighbor, his cousin, and his father. He said: We saw one who killed his father in the time of the Azariqah."
"7239","(7235): Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abd al-A’la al-Nakha’i, from Umm Abd Allah, who said: Abu Musa said to me in his illness: Shall I not inform you whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed? I said: Yes. He said: He cursed whoever shaves, wails loudly, or tears garments."
"7240","(7236): Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three days after Khaybar was opened, and he gave us a share, giving to none who had not witnessed the conquest except us."
"7241","(7237): Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Abu Musa, I think he raised it, saying: The likeness of the believer who recites the Qur’an is like the citron, its fragrance is pleasant and its taste pleasant; the likeness of the believer who does not recite the Qur’an is like the date, it has no fragrance and its taste is sweet; the likeness of the hypocrite who recites the Qur’an is like basil, its fragrance pleasant and its taste bitter; and the likeness of the hypocrite who does not recite the Qur’an is like the colocynth, it has no fragrance and its taste is bitter."
"7242","(7238): Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ash’ari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been given the openings and endings of speech. We said: O Messenger of Allah, teach us of what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, taught you. So he taught us the tashahhud."
"7243","(7239): Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa al-Ash’ari narrated to me, meaning from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, there are drinks there; what of them shall I drink and what leave? He said: What are they? I said: Bit’ and mizr. He said: What are bit’ and mizr? I said: Bit’ is of honey which becomes strong until it intoxicates, and mizr is of corn which becomes strong until it intoxicates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not drink an intoxicant, for I have forbidden every intoxicant."
"7244","(7240): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar ibn Maysarah al-Jushami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, Abu Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Musa, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and two men of the Ash’aris, one on my right and the other on my left, and both asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for office while he was using the siwak. He said: What do you say, O Abd Allah ibn Qays, or O Abu Musa? He said: By the One who sent you with truth, they did not inform me of what was in themselves, and I did not feel they sought office. It is as if I look at his siwak under his lip withdrawn. Then he said: O Abu Musa, we do not, or shall never, employ upon our work one who seeks it. But go you, O Abd Allah ibn Qays, or O Abu Musa. So he sent him to Yemen, then followed him with Mu’adh ibn Jabal. When he came to him, he said to him: Dismount, and cast a cushion for him."
"7245","(7241): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Sayyar Abu al-Hakam narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of Yemen make a drink, bit’ of honey, and mizr of corn and barley. He said: I forbid you every intoxicant."
"7246","(7242): Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Isra’il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: The wife of Ibn Maz’un entered upon the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they saw her of bad appearance. They said to her: What is wrong with you? There is no man in Quraysh richer than your husband. She said: We have had nothing of him: as for his day he fasts, and as for his night he stands. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and they mentioned that to him. He met him and said: O Uthman, do you not have an example in me? He said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you? He said: As for you, you stand at night and fast by day; your family has a right over you, and your body has a right over you. So pray and sleep, fast and break fast. Then the woman came to them after that perfumed as if a bride. They said to her: What happened? She said: We got what people get."
"7247","(7243): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, from Abu Bakr, from his father Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a stone were thrown into Hell it would fall seventy autumns before reaching its bottom."
"7248","(7244): Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A’mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to name himself names for us, saying: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of mercy, and the Prophet of battle."
"7249","(7245): Bundar narrated to us, Muhammad narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Murrah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Many men attained perfection, but of women none attained perfection but Maryam daughter of Imran and Asiyah wife of Pharaoh; and the superiority of A’ishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over all food."
"7250","(7246): Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Harb ibn Surayj, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, who said: I supped with Abu Burdah, and he said: Shall I not narrate to you what my father Abd Allah ibn Qays narrated to me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats and is satisfied, drinks and is quenched, then says: Praise belongs to Allah who fed me and satisfied me, gave me drink and quenched me, exits his sins as the day his mother bore him."
"7251","(7247): Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, who said: Abu Musa narrated, while at al-Dayr of Isfahan, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour is harj. We said: What is harj? He said: Killing. We said: By Allah, we kill in one year more than seventy thousand of the polytheists. He said: By Allah, it is not your killing the polytheists, but it is killing one another. We said: And among us is the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and with us our intellects? He said: And among you is the Book of Allah. You think your intellects are with you, except that the intellects of most of the people of that time will be taken away; they will think they are upon something while upon nothing, and there will remain a froth of people who think they are upon something while upon nothing. We said: What is the escape from that? He said: I find no escape for me and you from it, if it reaches us, in what our Prophet, upon him be peace, entrusted to us, except that we exit it as the day we entered it."
"7252","(7248): Muhammad ibn Isma’il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Mu’tamir narrated to us, saying: I read to Fudayl, from Abu Hariz, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None who persists in wine enters Paradise, nor one who believes in magic, nor one who severs; and whoever dies drinking wine, Allah gives him to drink of al-Ghutah, which is water flowing from the privates of prostitutes, whose stench harms those in the Fire."
"7253","(7249): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, al-Azhar ibn Sinan al-Qurashi informed us, Muhammad ibn Wasi’ al-Azdi narrated to us, saying: I entered upon Bilal ibn Abi Burdah and said to him: O Bilal, your father narrated to me from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: In Hell is a valley called Habhab; it is binding upon Allah to lodge in it every tyrant. So beware, O Bilal, lest you be of those who lodge in it."
"7254","(7250): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma’il, from Taliq ibn Imran ibn Husayn, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever separates a parent and child, and a brother and his brother."
"7255","(7251): Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of Ash’aris seeking mounts. He said: By Allah, I shall not mount you, and I have nothing to mount you upon. We stayed as Allah willed, then camels were brought, and he ordered for us three white-humped pairs. When we departed we said, or some said to others: Allah will not bless us; we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts, he swore not to mount us, then mounted us. Go to him and inform him. He said: I did not mount you, but Allah mounted you. By Allah, if Allah wills, I never swear an oath and see another better than it but I expiate my oath and do what is better."
"7256","(7252): Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; when the people ascended a height they said takbir. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you do not call upon one deaf nor absent, but you call upon One Hearing, Near. He came upon me while I said: There is no power nor strength except in Allah. He said: Yes, O Abd Allah, shall I not guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? There is no power nor strength except in Allah."
"7257","(7253): Muhriz ibn Awn narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-A’mash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights for bravery, fights for zeal, and fights for show; which of that is in the path of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"7258","(7254): Abu Hisham al-Rifa’i Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Amr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: An Arab Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he honored him, saying to him: Come to us. He came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask your need. He said: A she-camel to ride, and goats for my family to milk. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were you unable to be like the old woman of Banu Isra’il? When Musa traveled with Banu Isra’il from Egypt they lost the way. He said: What is this? Their scholars said: When death came to Yusuf he took a covenant upon us by Allah not to leave Egypt until we carry his bones with us. He said: Who knows the place of his grave? They said: An old woman of Banu Isra’il. He sent for her and she came. He said: Guide me to Yusuf’s grave. She said: Until you grant me my judgment. He said: What is your judgment? She said: That I be with you in Paradise. He disliked granting her that, so Allah revealed to him to grant her judgment. She set out with them to a lake, a place of stagnant water, and said: Drain this water. They drained it. She said: Dig and extract Yusuf’s bones. When they lifted them to the ground, the road was like daylight."
"7259","(7255): Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Hazm narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Abu Musa, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Before the Hour is harj. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Killing. They said: Does not what we kill every year, a hundred thousand of the polytheists, suffice? He said: Not that, but killing yourselves. They said: And with us our intellects? He said: The intellects of the people of that time will be snatched, and there will remain a froth of people who think they are upon something while upon nothing. Abu Musa said: I see it will only reach me and you; I know no exit from it in what was entrusted to us except that we exit it as the day we entered it."
"7260","(7256): Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, Salih ibn Salih ibn Hayy al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Sha’bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever has a slave girl and disciplines her, disciplines her well, teaches her and teaches her well, then frees her and marries her, has two rewards; and any man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet and believed in Muhammad has two rewards; and any slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters has two rewards. Salih said: al-Sha’bi said to me: I gave it to you for nothing, though a rider would ride for less than it to Madinah."
"7261","(7257): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Burayd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: He came to Umar and stood at his door, saying: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah; is Abu Musa, or Abd Allah ibn Qays, permitted? Three times, but he was not answered, so he left. Umar came out and said: Where is Abu Musa? They said: He left. He sent after him; when he came he said: What turned you away? He said: I sought permission three times and was not permitted, so I left; and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him leave. He said: Bring me with you one who heard this from him. So he came to the Ansar and informed them; all said: We heard it. He said: Let some of you stand with me. Some stood with him and came to Umar and informed them."
"7262","(7258): And from Abu Musa, who said: Some people of my tribe came to me and said: Seek mounts for us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he provides mounts upon camels. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought mounts. He swore: By Allah, I shall not mount you. We left grieved thereby. We stayed days, and camels were brought. He said: Take these two pairs, take these two pairs, three times, six loads. I said to my companions: He swore not to mount us, and I see only that he forgot. If we take them they will not be blessed for us. We said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore three times not to mount us? He said: And I swear now, by Allah I shall surely mount you. He swore three times, then said: Whoever swears an oath and sees what is better than it, let him do what is better and expiate his oath."
"7263","(7259): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza’i, from Musa ibn Sulayman, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Musa, who said: I watched for the breaking of the Prophet’s fast and brought him jar nabidh. When he brought it near his mouth it fizzed, so he said: Strike this against the wall, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in Allah nor the Last Day."
"7264","(7260): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Sadaqah Abu Muawiyah, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah informing that he brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) jar nabidh, and he said to him the like of this."
"7265","(7261): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Burayd narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who bears arms against us."
"7266","(7262): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki’ narrated to us, from al-Mas’udi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not sleep, nor is it fitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it. His veil is light; if He uncovered it, the splendors of His face would burn everything His sight reached of His creation. Then Abu Ubaydah recited: Blessed is whoever is in the fire and whoever is around it, and glory belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"7267","(7263): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-A’mash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, except he did not mention: And Abu Ubaydah recited."
"7268","(7264): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"7269","(7265): Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abu Jamrah al-Duba’i narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the two cool prayers enters Paradise."
"7270","(7266): Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: O my son, had you seen us with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when rain befell us, you would have thought our smell was the smell of sheep."
"7271","(7267): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Burayd narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from his father Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, who said: He came as a delegation to Umar, or to Sulayman. He fulfilled his needs; then in part of the night he said: Stand. He stood and went to the ruler’s door and knocked. The chamberlain said: Who is this? Abu Burdah said: Seek permission for me. He entered and informed him of his place, so he came out and permitted him. He said: Good news, O Abu Burdah? He said: Good. He said: Your need? He said: I finished my needs; I remembered a hadith: (7268): My father narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers creation for reckoning, a Jew or a Christian is brought, and it is said: O believer, this is your ransom from the Fire. He said: Did you hear it? He said: I heard it from my father."
"7272","(7269): Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah al-Hamdani, from Murrah, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many men attained perfection, but of women none attained perfection but Maryam daughter of Imran and Asiyah wife of Pharaoh; and the superiority of A’ishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over all food."
"7273","(7270): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Burayd narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truthful companion and the evil companion are like the carrier of musk: either he gives you, or you find a pleasant scent; and the blower of the bellows either burns your clothes or you find a foul scent."
"7274","(7271): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Isma’il narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets passed by the rock of al-Rawha’ barefoot, wearing cloaks."
"7275","(7272): Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Abu Ja’far al-Razi, Rabi’ ibn Anas narrated to us, from his two grandfathers Zayd and Ziyad, who used to visit Abu Musa at Basra to recite the Qur’an to him, from Abu Musa, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The prayer of a man is not accepted while anything of it remains in his skin or body, meaning yellowness."
"7276","(7273): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu’tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abbad, from Abu Mijlaz, from Abu Musa, who said: We brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ablution water, and he performed ablution, saying: O Allah, forgive my sin, widen my house for me, and bless my provision for me."
"7277","(7274): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ja’far ibn Burqan, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: Two men of Hadramawt disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land. He said to the defendant: Swear. The claimant said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but his oath? Then he will take my land. He said: If he takes it by his oath, he will be of those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not speak to, does not look at, does not purify, and for him is a painful punishment. So the other held back and returned it to him."
"7278","(7275): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mu’alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Musa ibn A’yan, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Uqayl, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Abu Musa, who said: I and Abu al-Darda’ were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his legs enters Paradise."
"7279","(7276): Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Mujammi’ ibn Yahya, from Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from his father, who said: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said: If only we sat until we pray Isha with him. We sat, and he came out to us and said: Have you remained here? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we prayed Maghrib with you, then said: We shall sit until we pray Isha with you. He said: You did well, or you did right. He raised his head to the sky, and he often raised his head to the sky, and said: The stars are a security for the people of heaven; when the stars go, there comes to the people of heaven what they are promised. I am a security for my Companions; when I go, there comes to my Companions what they are promised. My Companions are a security for my nation; when my Companions go, there comes to my nation what they are promised."
"7280","(7277): Abu Hisham al-Rifa’i narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation is a nation shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter; its punishment is in this world: earthquakes, tribulations, and killing."
"7281","(7278): al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Ayyub ibn A’idh narrated to us, Qays ibn Muslim narrated to us, I heard Tariq ibn Shihab saying: Abu Musa al-Ash’ari narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to my people’s land; I came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was camped at al-Abtah. I greeted him. He said: Did you perform Hajj, O Abd Allah ibn Qays? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What did you say? I said: I said: Here I am with an ihram like your ihram. He said: Did you drive a sacrificial animal? I said: No, I did not drive one. He said: Circumambulate the House and run between al-Safa, then exit ihram. I did so until a woman of Banu Qays combed me. We remained so until Umar was made caliph. I was at the Station giving fatwa to people by what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me and what I did. A man came and whispered in my ear: Go slow in your fatwa, for the Commander of the Faithful has innovated in the rites. I said: O people, whomever we gave fatwa to about the rites, let him go slow, for this Commander of the Faithful is coming to you; to me whoever learned anything of him. When Umar came I said: O Commander of the Faithful, did you innovate in the rites? He said: If we take by the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it commands us completion; and if we take by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he did not exit ihram until he sacrificed the camels. So he forbade Umrah in the days of Hajj."
"7282","(7279): Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nafi’ narrated to us, Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and A’ishah passed by Abu Musa while he recited in his house; they stood listening to his recitation, then went on. In the morning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abu Musa and said: O Abu Musa, I passed by you last night with A’ishah while you recited in your house; we stood and listened. Abu Musa said to him: As for me, O Messenger of Allah, had I known I would have beautified it for you."
"7283","(7280): Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, that two men claimed a camel, each bringing two witnesses, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it between them."
"7284","(7281): Hudbah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Sa’id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim dies but Allah places in his place a man of the Jews or Christians in the Fire."
"7285","(7282): Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Ma’shar narrated to us, from Mus’ab ibn Thabit, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer but comes on the Day of Resurrection with a Jew or Christian, saying: This is my ransom from the Fire."
"7286","(7283): al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Sa’id Rawh ibn Janah narrated to us, from a freedman of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Day the shin is uncovered. He said: Of a great light before which they fall prostrate."
"7287","(7284): Ibrahim ibn Sa’id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of Banu Isra’il was stricter in urine than you; he had a chisel with him, and when urine touched any of his body he scraped it with it."
"7288","(7285): Ibrahim ibn Sa’id narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant who transgressed against himself than a man traveling in a barren destructive wasteland; when in its midst he lost his mount, sought it right and left until wearied, or despaired of it, and thought he perished, he looked and found it in a place he did not hope to find it. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is more joyful at the repentance of His transgressing servant than that man with his mount when he found it."
"7289","(7286): And from Abu Musa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which Muslims are best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe."
"7290","(7287): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives respite to the wrongdoer until when He seizes him he does not escape. Then he recited: Such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing; indeed His seizure is painful, severe."
"7291","(7288): Sa’id ibn Yahya ibn Sa’id al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, Abu Burdah narrated to us, from Abu Musa, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which Islam is best? He said: One from whose tongue and hand Muslims are safe."
"7292","(7289): al-Qawariri narrated to us, Makki narrated to us, from al-Ju’ayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Humayd ibn Bashir, from Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, who said: Abu Musa al-Ash’ari narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man turns its dice looking at what it brings but he disobeys Allah and His Messenger."
"7293","(7290): Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Jushami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa’id and Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi’, from Sa’id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays with backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"7294","(7291): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you passes in our mosque or our market with arrows, let him hold their blades, or he said: let him grasp with his palm lest any Muslim be struck by anything of them."
"7295","(7292): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"7296","(7293): And from Abu Musa, who said: A house burned in Madinah at night over its people; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of them, he said: This fire is but an enemy to you; when you sleep, extinguish it from you."
"7297","(7294): And from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest of people in reward for prayer are the farthest of them in walking to it, then the farthest; and one who waits for prayer until he prays it with the imam in congregation is greater in reward than one who prays it then sleeps."
"7298","(7295): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"7299","(7296): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a beggar came to him, and perhaps he said: A beggar or one in need came, he said: Intercede and be rewarded, and Allah decrees upon the tongue of His Prophet what He wills."
"7300","(7297): And from Abu Musa, who said: My companions sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him mounts for them when they were in the army of hardship, the expedition of Tabuk. I said: O Prophet of Allah, my companions sent me to you to mount them. He said: No, by Allah, I shall not mount them upon anything. I found him angry unknowingly. I returned grieved at the refusal of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and fearing he held something against me. I returned to my companions and informed them what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. I stayed only a short while when I heard Bilal calling: Where is Abd Allah ibn Qays? I answered him. He said: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he calls you. When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Take these two pairs, these two pairs, and these two pairs, six camels he had then bought from Sa’d, and go with them to your companions and say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mounts you upon these, so ride them. Abu Musa said: I went to my companions with them and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounts you upon these; but by Allah I shall not leave you until some of you go with me to those who heard the words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I asked him for you, and his refusal the first time, then his giving them to me after, lest you think I told you something he did not say. They said: By Allah, you are trusted with us, and we shall do what you like. So Abu Musa went with some of them until they came to those who heard the words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his refusal, then his giving after; and they narrated to them the like of what Abu Musa narrated, exactly."
"7301","(7298): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I saw in a dream that I migrate from Makkah to a land with date palms; my thought went to Yamamah and Hajar, but it is Madinah, Yathrib. And I saw in this dream of mine that I shook a sword and its upper part broke; it was what befell the believers on the day of Uhud. I shook it again and it returned better than before; it was what Allah brought of conquest and gathering of believers. And I saw in it cows, and Allah is best; they are the group of believers on the day of Uhud. And the good is what Allah brought of good after, and the reward of truth came to us after, on the day of Badr."
"7302","(7299): And from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will surely come when a man circles with charity of gold, then finds none to take it from him; and a man is seen followed by forty women clinging to him, due to few men and many women."
"7303","(7300): And from Abu Musa, who said: I and my companions who came with me in the ship stayed at Baqi’ Buthan, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Madinah; a group of them took turns visiting the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Isha prayer every night. Abu Musa said: We coincided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my companions, while he was occupied with some matter; he delayed the prayer until the night darkened. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and finished his prayer, he said to those present: Stay calm; rejoice, for of Allah’s favor upon you is that none of the people prays this prayer but you, or he said: None prayed this hour but you. He does not know which of the two phrases he said. Abu Musa said: We returned rejoicing at what we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7304","(7301): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"7305","(7302): And from Abu Musa, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he stood praying with the longest standing, bowing, and prostration I ever saw him do in any prayer, then said: These signs sent are not for anyone’s death nor life, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends them to frighten His servants thereby. When you see anything of them, hasten to His remembrance, supplication, and seeking forgiveness."
"7306","(7303): And from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about things he disliked; when they pressed him he became angry, then said to people: Ask me whatever you wish. A man said: Who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. Another said: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Salim, freedman of Shaybah. When Umar saw the anger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Messenger of Allah, we repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"7307","(7304): And from Abu Musa, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a campaign, six of us with one camel we rode in turns. Our feet wore out, my feet wore out, and my nails fell. We wrapped rags on our feet. It was named the expedition of Dhat al-Riqa’ for what we bound on our feet of rags. Abu Burdah said: Abu Musa narrated this hadith, then disliked that, saying: What was I to do mentioning this hadith? Because he disliked that anything of his deed be disclosed. Abu Usamah said, and others said: Allah rewards for it."
"7308","(7305): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Keep to the Qur’an, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it escapes more than camels from their hobbles."
"7309","(7306): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the house in which Allah is remembered and the house in which Allah is not remembered is like the living and the dead."
"7310","(7307): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the righteous companion and the evil companion is like the carrier of musk and the blower of the bellows: the carrier of musk either gives you, or you buy from him, or you find from him a pleasant scent; and the blower of the bellows either burns your clothes or you find from him a stinking scent."
"7311","(7308): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: For the slave who perfects worship of his Lord and renders to his master what is due upon him of right, counsel, and obedience, are two rewards: the reward of perfecting worship of his Lord, and the reward of rendering to his owner what is due upon him of right."
"7312","(7309): And with the same chain from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Ash’aris run short of provisions in a campaign, or their families’ food in Madinah becomes little, they gather what they have in one cloth, then divide among themselves in one vessel equally; they are of me and I am of them."
"7313","(7310): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: My likeness and what Allah sent me with is like a man whose people came to him and said: O people, I saw the army; I am the naked warner, so escape! A group of his people obeyed him and set out early, proceeding leisurely, and were saved; a group denied, remaining in their place, and the army attacked them at dawn and destroyed them. That is the likeness of whoever obeys me and follows what I came with, and whoever disobeys me and denies what I came with of truth."
"7314","(7311): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of what Allah brought me of guidance and knowledge is like rain that fell upon land: part of it was good, accepting water, producing abundant herbage and grass; part of it were reservoirs holding water, by which Allah benefited people, drinking, watering, and planting; and part of it was another tract, only hollows holding no water nor producing herbage. That is the likeness of one who understood the religion of Allah and benefited by what Allah sent me with, learning and teaching; and the likeness of one who did not raise his head thereby nor accepted Allah’s guidance with which I was sent."
"7315","(7312): And from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of Muslims, Jews, and Christians is like a man who hired people to work for him a day till night for a known wage. They worked for him till midday, then said: We need not your wage you stipulated for us, and what we did is void. He said to them: Do not do so; work the rest of your day and take your wage complete. They refused and left that upon him. He hired others after them, saying: Work the rest of your day and yours is what I stipulated for them of wage. They worked until when it was Asr time, they said: What we did is void for you, and yours is the wage you made for us; we need it not. He said: Work the rest of your work, for what remains of the day is little, then take your wage. They refused him. He hired others, who worked for him the rest of their day until the sun set, completing the wage of both groups, and all the wage. That is the likeness of the Jews and Christians and those who abandoned what Allah commanded them, and the likeness of the Muslims who accepted Allah’s guidance and what His Messenger brought."
"7316","(7313): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished Hunayn, he sent Abu Amir with an army to Awtas. He met Durayd ibn al-Simmah, killed Durayd, and Allah defeated his companions. Abu Musa said: And he sent me with Abu Amir. Abu Amir was shot in his knee; a man of Banu Jusham shot him with an arrow, lodging it in his knee. I reached him and said: O uncle, who shot you? Abu Amir pointed to Abu Musa: That is my killer, you see him who shot me. Abu Musa said: I made for him, headed for him, and caught up with him. When he saw me he turned away fleeing, and I followed him, saying: Have you no shame? Will you not stand? Have you no shame? Are you not an Arab? He stopped. I and he met, we exchanged two blows, and I struck him with the sword and killed him. Then I returned to Abu Amir and said: Allah has killed your man. He said: Pull out this arrow. I pulled it, and water came out of it. He said: O son of my brother, go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), convey my greeting to him, and say to him: He says to you: Seek forgiveness for me. Abu Amir left me in charge, stayed a little, then died. When I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I entered upon him while he was in a house upon a bed, and the bed had left marks on the back and sides of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I informed him our news and Abu Amir’s news, saying: He said: Seek forgiveness for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, performed ablution from it, raised his hands, then said: O Allah, forgive Ubayd, Abu Amir. Then said: O Allah, make him on the Day of Resurrection above many of Your creation and of people. I said: And for me, O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Abd Allah ibn Qays his sin, and admit him a noble admission. Abu Burdah said: One is for Abu Amir and the other for Abu Musa."
"7317","(7314): And from Abu Musa, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), camped at al-Ji’ranah between Makkah and Madinah, with Bilal with him. An Arab Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: Will you not fulfill for me, O Muhammad, what you promised me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Rejoice. The Bedouin said to him: You have given me much rejoicing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Musa and Bilal as an angry one, saying: He has rejected the glad tidings, so accept you two. They said: We accept, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a cup with water, washed his hands and face, spat into it, then said to them: Drink from it, pour over your faces and necks. They took the cup and did what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them. Umm Salamah called to us from behind the curtain to leave some of what was in their vessel for their mother, so they left some for her."
"7318","(7315): And from Abu Musa, who said: A boy was born to me; I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He named him Ibrahim, did tahnik with a date, supplicated for blessing for him, handed him to me; and he was the eldest child of Abu Musa."
"7319","(7316): And from Abu Musa, who said: News of the emergence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us while we were in Yemen; we set out migrating to him, my two brothers, I the youngest: one Abu Burdah, the other Abu Ruhm, in some fifty men of my people. We boarded a ship, and our ship cast us to the Negus in Abyssinia, where we found Ja’far ibn Abi Talib and his companions with him. Ja’far said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us and ordered us to stay, so stay with us. We stayed with him until we all came. We found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the opening of Khaybar; he gave us a share, or said: gave us of it. He gave nothing to anyone absent from a conquest, meaning Khaybar, except those who witnessed it with him, except our ship companions with Ja’far and his companions; he divided for them with them. Some people said to us, meaning the ship people: We preceded you in migration. Asma’ daughter of Umays, who came with us, entered upon Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), visiting; she had migrated to the Negus among those who migrated to him. Umar entered upon Hafsah with Asma’ with her. Umar said when he saw Asma’: Who is this? She said: Asma’ daughter of Umays. Umar said: This Abyssinian? This seafarer? Asma’ said: Yes. Umar said: We preceded you in migration; we are more entitled to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She became angry and said a word: O Umar, no, by Allah; you were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he fed your hungry and admonished your ignorant, while we were in the land, or the land of the distant hated ones, in Abyssinia, and that for Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By Allah, I shall taste no food nor drink any drink until I mention what you said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We were harmed and frightened, and I shall mention that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him; by Allah I shall not lie, nor deviate, nor add to that. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, she said: O Prophet of Allah, Umar said such and such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you say to him? She said: I said such and such. He said: He is not more entitled to me than you; he and his companions have one migration, while you, people of the ship, have two migrations. She said: I saw Abu Musa and the ship companions coming to me in groups asking me about this hadith; nothing of this world delights them nor is greater in themselves than what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Abu Burdah said: Asma’ said: I saw Abu Musa repeatedly asking me for this hadith. (7317): And he narrated another time, saying: Yours is migration twice: you migrated to the Negus and you migrated to me."
"7320","(7318): And from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I recognize the voices of the company of Ash’aris with the Qur’an, though I do not see their dwellings when they camp by day, and I recognize their dwellings by their voices with the Qur’an by night; among them is Hakim, when he meets the cavalry, or he said: the enemy, he says to them: My companions order you to wait for them."
"7321","(7319): And from Abu Musa, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent one of his Companions on some matter, he said: Give glad tidings and do not repel, make easy and do not make difficult."
"7322","(7320): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Burayd narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and two men of my cousins. One of the two men said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint us over some of what Allah entrusted you with. The other said the like. He said: By Allah, we do not appoint to this work one who asks for it, nor one who covets it."
"7323","(7321): And from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other; then he interlaced his fingers."
"7324","(7322): Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Burayd, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah gives respite to the wrongdoer until when He seizes him He does not let him go. Then he recited: Such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing; indeed His seizure is painful, severe."
"7325","(7323): Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha’bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a slave girl and is good to her, disciplines her, frees her, and marries her, has two rewards."
"7326","Ishaq narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abu 'Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Qays who said: I heard my father, while in the presence of the enemy, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed the gates of Paradise are beneath the shadows of the swords."" He said: Then a man from the people, shabby in appearance, stood up and said: O Abu Musa, did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: Then he returned to his companions and said: I bid you farewell with peace, then he broke the scabbard of his sword and threw it away, then he walked with his sword toward the enemy and fought until he was killed."
"7327","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Visit the sick, feed the hungry, and free the captive,"" meaning the prisoner."
"7328","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr Abu Ghallab, from Hittan ibn 'Abdullah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""When he says Allahu Akbar — meaning the imam — then say Allahu Akbar, and when he recites, then listen attentively."""
"7329","'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Zurarah al-Hadrami al-Kufi, trustworthy, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The orphan girl is to be consulted concerning herself; if she remains silent then she has given permission, and if she refuses she is not to be coerced."""
"7330","'Abdullah ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"7331","'Asim ibn al-Nadr al-Ahwal narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, Abu 'Uthman narrated to us, from Anas ibn Jandal — Anas narrates that he — heard from Abu Musa, saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke of a tribulation in which the one sleeping is better than the one sitting, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one hastening, or as he said."
"7332","Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Harawi narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa who said: I heard Abu Musa say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The gates of Paradise are beneath the shadows of the swords."" He said: Then a man shabby in appearance said: O Abu Musa, did you yourself hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: Then he came to his companions and said: I bid you farewell with peace, then he broke the scabbard of his sword, then he threw it toward the enemy, and struck with it until he was killed."
"7333","Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-'Ammi narrated to us, Abu 'Imran narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Qays, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Two gardens of silver, their vessels and whatever is in them, and two gardens of gold, their vessels and whatever is in them, and there is nothing between the people and looking at their Lord — Mighty and Majestic — except the cloak of grandeur over His face in the Garden of Eden."""
"7334","And from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed in Paradise there is a tent of hollow pearl, its width sixty miles; in every corner of it are people whom the others do not see; the believer will go around to them."""
"7335","Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Umays ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated to me, from Qays ibn Muslim al-Jadali, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa who said: The day of 'Ashura was a day the Jews fasted and venerated, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he commanded fasting it."
"7336","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shu'bah — or Sa'id — narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Masruq ibn Aws: that Abu Musa narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the fingers ten each."
"7337","Ishaq narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Masruq ibn Aws, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the fingers ten each."
"7338","Musnad of 'Amr ibn al-'As, may Allah be pleased with him. And with it Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed us, reading to him, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Janzarudhi informed us, reading to him, Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us, with Abu Ja'far al-'Aza'imi reading to him in Rajab in the year 375, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy, from his father who said: I heard 'Amr ibn al-'As say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Tighten your clothes upon you."" He said: So I did, then I came to him and found him performing ablution, so he raised his head and looked me up and down, then said: ""O 'Amr, I intend to send you on an expedition, so Allah will keep you safe and grant you spoils, and I desire for you a righteous share of wealth."" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not embrace Islam out of desire for wealth; I embraced Islam only out of desire for jihad and to be with you. So he said: ""O 'Amr, how excellent is righteous wealth for a righteous man."""
"7339","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ulayy, from his father, from Abu Qays, freedman of 'Amr ibn al-'As, from 'Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The difference between your fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the meal of suhur."""
"7340","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Matar, from Raja', from Qabisah, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: Do not confuse for us the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the waiting period of the umm walad is the waiting period of the woman whose husband has died."
"7341","'Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: I never saw Quraysh intend to kill the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except on the day they conspired against him while they were sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at the Maqam. Then 'Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt stood up to him and put his cloak around his neck, then pulled it until he fell to his knees, and the people shouted, thinking he had been killed. He said: And Abu Bakr came hastening until he took hold of the upper arm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind, saying: Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah?! Then they turned away from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and when he finished his prayer he passed by them while they were sitting in the shade of the Ka'bah, and said: ""O assembly of Quraysh, by the One in whose hand is my soul, I have only been sent to you with slaughter,"" and he gestured with his hand to his throat. Abu Jahl said to him: O Muhammad, you were never ignorant. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You are among them."""
"7342","Abu Bakr narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and stood, then said: ""Those before you perished only by questioning their prophets and disagreeing with them; no one will truly believe until he believes in the whole of the decree, its good and its evil."""
"7343","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam who said: I heard Dhakwan narrating, from a freedman of 'Amr ibn al-'As, that he sent to 'Ali asking permission to visit Asma' bint 'Umays, so he gave him permission, until when he had finished his need, the freedman asked 'Amr about that, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from entering upon women without the permission of their husbands."
"7344","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Warqa', from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ziyad, freedman of 'Amr ibn al-'As, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The rebellious party will kill 'Ammar."""
"7345","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Shadhan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Khatmi, from 'Umarah ibn Khuzaymah who said: We went out with 'Amr ibn al-'As heading toward Makkah, when we saw a woman wearing bangles and rings, who had stretched out her hand toward the litter. He said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we saw some crows — meaning among them a crow with a white blaze, red beak and feet — and he said: ""None of the women will enter Paradise except the like of this crow among these crows."""
"7346","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Shabbabah narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from a man, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A single man from among them may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims."""
"7347","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Jurayri, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is dearest to you? He said: ""'A'ishah."" He said: Among men? He said: ""Abu Bakr."" He said: Then whom? He said: ""Then Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."""
"7348","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm, from his father who said: 'Amr ibn Hazm entered upon 'Amr ibn al-'As and said: 'Ammar has been killed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The rebellious party will kill him."" So 'Amr entered upon Mu'awiyah and said: 'Ammar has been killed. Mu'awiyah said: 'Ammar has been killed, so what? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The rebellious party will kill him."" He said: You have slipped in your urine! Did we kill him? It was 'Ali and his companions who killed him."
"7349","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: Since we embraced Islam, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never equated anyone among his companions with me and with Khalid ibn al-Walid in his warfare."
"7350","al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya al-Qattan narrated to us, from Sulayman who said: I heard Abu Salih saying: 'Amr ibn al-'As came to the house of 'Ali seeking him, but could not find him; then he returned and found him. When he entered he spoke to Fatimah, so 'Ali said to him: I do not see your need being with the woman? He said: Yes indeed; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from entering upon women whose husbands are absent."
"7351","Abu Musa Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Harawi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Raja' ibn Haywah, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from 'Amr ibn al-'As who said: Do not confuse for us the Sunnah of our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the waiting period of the umm walad whose master has died from her is four months and ten days."
"7352","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn al-Ahnaf, who heard Abu Sallam al-Aswad saying: Abu Salih al-Ash'ari informed me that Abu 'Abdullah al-Ash'ari narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man who did not complete his bowing and prostration, and said: ""Had this one died in this state he would have died upon other than the religion of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So complete the bowing and the prostration, for the likeness of one who prays without completing his bowing and prostration is like the hungry one who eats only one date or two dates — they avail him nothing."" Abu Salih said: So I met Abu 'Abdullah and said: Who narrated this hadith to you as having heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The commanders of the armies narrated it to me: Khalid ibn al-Walid, Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, and 'Amr ibn al-'As, that they heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7353","Isma'il ibn Musa, son of the daughter of al-Suddi, narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal who said: I returned with Mu'awiyah from Siffin; Mu'awiyah and Abu al-A'war al-Sulami were riding on one side, and I saw them riding on one side, and I was between them with no one else. Sometimes I would hurry to these, and sometimes I would hurry to those. Then I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr saying to his father: Father, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to 'Ammar when he was building the mosque: ""You are keen for reward."" He said: Yes. He said: ""And you are of the people of Paradise, and the rebellious party will kill you."" He said: Yes, I heard it. He said: Then why did you kill him? He said: So he turned to Mu'awiyah and said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, do you not hear what this one says? He said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to 'Ammar while he was building the mosque: ""Woe to you, you are keen for reward, and the rebellious party will kill you""? He said: Yes, I heard it. He said: Then why did you kill him? He said: Woe to you, you keep slipping in your urine; did we kill him? It was only those who brought him who killed him."
"7354","Abu Ya'qub Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Ibn 'Awn narrated to us, from 'Umayr ibn Ishaq who said: Ja'far sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Permit me to go to a land where I may worship Allah fearing no one. So he permitted him, and he went to the Negus. He said: Then 'Amr ibn al-'As narrated to me, he said: When I saw his position I envied him. He said: I said: By Allah, I shall strive against this one and his companions. He said: So I went to the Negus and entered with him to him, and said: In your land there is a man whose cousin is in our land, and he claims that people have but one God, and by Allah, if you do not kill him and his companions, I shall never again bring this semen to you — neither I nor any of my companions. He said: Call him. I said: He will not come with me, so send a messenger with me. He said: So he came, and when he reached the door I called out: Permit 'Amr ibn al-'As. And he called out from behind me: Permit 'Ubaydullah. He said: So he heard his voice and permitted him before me. He said: So he and his companions entered. He said: Then he permitted me and I entered, and there he was sitting. He said: Then he mentioned where his seat was from the couch, and mentioned the hadith at length."
"7355","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather who said: 'Amr ibn al-'As said: An army of Muslims went out, I being their commander, until we camped at Alexandria. A chief among their chiefs said to me: Send out to me a man whom I may address and who may address me. So I said: None but I shall go out to him. So I went out with his interpreter until two pulpits were set for us. He said: Who are you? We said: We are the Arabs; we are the people of the thorn and the qaraz, and we are the people of the House of Allah. We were the people of the narrowest land and the hardest livelihood; we ate carrion and blood, and raided one another, with the worst livelihood people ever lived — until there emerged among us a man who was neither the noblest among us that day in honor nor the richest in wealth. He said: I am the Messenger of Allah to you. He commanded us with things we did not know and forbade us what we and our fathers had been upon. So we turned away from him, denied him, and rejected his word, until there went out to him a people other than us who said: We believe you and have faith in you and follow you and fight whoever fights you. So he went out to them, and we went out against him and fought him; he killed us and prevailed over us and overcame us, and took on the Arabs next to him and fought them until he prevailed over them. If those Arabs behind me knew the life you are in, none would remain but would come to you to share with you the life you are in. Then he laughed and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke truly. Our messengers came to us with the like of what your messenger brought, and we were upon it until kings arose among us who began acting in it according to their desires and abandoning the command of the prophets. So if you hold to the command of your prophet, none will fight you but you will overcome him, and none will contend with you but you will prevail over him. But if you do the like of what we did — abandoning the command of your prophet and acting like they acted according to their desires — we shall be left to face you, and you will be neither more numerous nor stronger than us. 'Amr ibn al-'As said: I never spoke to a more intelligent man than him."
"7356","Hadith of Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him. 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah who gives. Whomever I give a gift while my soul is content with it, it is blessed for him in it; and whomever I give a gift out of craving of soul and insistence in asking, he is like one who eats and is never satiated."""
"7357","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to me, Khalid ibn Hayyan Abu Yazid al-Kharraz narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zibriqan, from Ya'la ibn Aws who said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Every intoxicant is forbidden for every believer."""
"7358","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: 'Umar ibn 'Ata' informed me that Nafi' ibn Jubayr sent him to al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid to ask him. Al-Sa'ib said to him: I prayed Friday with Mu'awiyah in the maqsurah, and when I finished I stood to pray, so he said to me: When you pray Friday, do not join it to another prayer unless you speak or go out, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that."
"7359","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father who said: I heard Mu'awiyah saying while upon the pulpit, with a lock of hair in his hand: What is with your women putting things like this in their heads? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is no woman who puts hair other than her own upon her head except that it is falsehood."""
"7360","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"7361","Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar Abu Ayyub al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a man, from Mu'awiyah, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eat laba' (first milk), then pray without performing ablution."
"7362","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu al-Tayyah who said: I heard Humran ibn Aban saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan addressed us and said: You pray a prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never prayed, and he forbade it — meaning the two rak'ahs after 'Asr."
"7363","Abu Hammam narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to me, he said: Ibn Abi al-Muhajir — or Abu 'Abd Rabb, al-Walid doubted — narrated to me, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A man among those before you met a learned man — or a worshipper — and said: The other one killed ninety-nine souls, all of them wrongfully; do you find any repentance for me? He said: No. So he killed him. Then he met another and said: The other one killed a hundred souls, all of them wrongfully; do you find any repentance for me? He said: If I told you that Allah — Mighty and Majestic — does not accept the repentance of one who repents, I would have lied. There is a monastery here in which people worship; go to them and worship Allah with them — perhaps Allah will accept your repentance. So he set out to them but died before reaching them. Then the angels of punishment and the angels of mercy disputed, so Allah sent an angel: Measure between the two places, and whichever he is nearer to, he belongs to it. So they measured and found him nearer to the monastery of the repentant by a finger-breadth, so Allah forgave him."""
"7364","Abu Hammam narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir who said: I heard Abu 'Abd Rabb saying: I heard Mu'awiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Deeds are only by their endings, like a vessel: when its top is good, its bottom is good, and when its top is bad, its bottom is bad."""
"7365","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; if he returns, then kill him."""
"7366","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Jarir saying: I heard a shaykh narrating to Mughirah, from the daughter of Hisham ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah — who used to nurse 'Ammar — she said: Mu'awiyah came to 'Ammar to visit him in illness. When he left him he said: O Allah, do not make his death at our hands, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The rebellious party will kill 'Ammar."""
"7367","'Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Mujammi', from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf who said: I heard Mu'awiyah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and he heard the mu'adhdhin and said the like of what he said."
"7368","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Janah, from Ibn Halbas, from Mu'awiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You claim that I am among the last of you to die; rather I am among the first of you to die, and you will follow me in scattered groups, striking one another's necks."""
"7369","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."""
"7370","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hakam ibn Mina', from Zayd ibn Jariyah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"7371","'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Hanafiyyah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The 'umra (life-grant) is valid for its recipients."""
"7372","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj ibn Hurmuz narrated to me that al-'Abbas ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-'Abbas married 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam to his daughter, and 'Abd al-Rahman married him to his daughter, and they had made that the dowry. So Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan — while caliph — wrote to Marwan and commanded him to separate them, saying in his letter: This is shighar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"7373","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Hariz ibn 'Uthman who said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi 'Awf al-Jurashi narrated to me, from Abu Hind al-Bajali, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Emigration will not cease until repentance ceases"" — he said it three times — ""and repentance will not cease until the sun rises from its west."""
"7374","Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Antaki narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from 'Atiyyah ibn Qays who said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The eye is the stopper of the anus; when the eye sleeps, the stopper comes loose."""
"7375","Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Antaki narrated to us, Mubashshir — meaning Ibn Isma'il al-Halabi al-Kalbi — and al-Harith ibn 'Atiyyah and Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ya'ish ibn al-Walid, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I entered upon Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying in a single garment. So I said: Do I see him praying as I see? She said: Yes — and it is the garment in which was what was."
"7376","Abu 'Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman Abu al-'Ala' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Kaysan, freedman of Mu'awiyah, who said: Mu'awiyah addressed us and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade seven things, and I forbid you them. Indeed among them are: wailing, singing, images, poetry, gold, skins of beasts of prey, displaying adornment, and silk."
"7377","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies with no imam over him dies a death of ignorance."""
"7378","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ghamr, freedman of Sumuk, narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, who said: I heard Mu'awiyah ibn Hudayj say: I was with Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan when the letter of his governor came to him informing him that he had fallen upon the Turks and defeated them, and of the many he killed among them and the much booty he took. Mu'awiyah became angry at that, then ordered it written to him: I have understood what you mentioned of what you killed and seized; let me not learn that you return to any of that, nor fight them until my order comes to you. I said to him: Why, O Commander of the Believers? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The Turks will surely prevail over the Arabs until they drive them back to the growths of shih and qaysum (desert plants)."" So I dislike fighting them for that reason."
"7379","Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will be rulers against whom no objection is raised; they will plunge into the Fire, one following another."""
"7380","al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Sa'ib ibn Hubaysh al-Kala'i, from Abu al-Shammakh al-Azdi, from a cousin of his who had companionship, that he entered upon Mu'awiyah and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever is put in charge of anything of the Muslims and closes his door to the needy, the weak, and the one in need, to their needs and poverty — Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will close the door of His mercy to him on the day of his need and poverty, when he is most in need of that."" I do not know who said: — whether al-Azdi to Mu'awiyah, or Mu'awiyah to al-Azdi — I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7381","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far Ghundar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd al-Bajali, from Jarir, that he heard Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan delivering a sermon, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died at sixty-three, and Abu Bakr died, and 'Umar, at sixty-three."
"7382","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from his grandfather Sa'id ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, from Mu'awiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution."" He said: When he performed ablution he looked at me and said: ""O Mu'awiyah, if you are put in charge of a matter, fear Allah and be just."" He said: I never ceased thinking I would be afflicted with office because of the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until I was put in charge."
"7383","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Thawr, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is neither overpowered nor deceived, nor informed of what He does not know. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in the religion; and whomever He does not give understanding, He pays him no mind."""
"7384","Abu Ya'la informed us, he said: I found in my book, from Suwayd — though I did not see upon it the mark of hearing, and upon it was 'sahh' (correct), so I doubted it, though my strongest supposition is that I heard it from him — from Dimam ibn Isma'il al-Ma'afiri, from Abu Qabil who said: Mu'awiyah addressed us on a Friday and said: Wealth is but our wealth and the fay' is but our fay'; whomever we wish we give, and whomever we wish we withhold. And no one answered him. When the second Friday came he said the like of his saying, and no one answered him. When the third Friday came he said the like of his saying, and a man among those present in the mosque stood up to him and said: Nay! Wealth is but our wealth and the fay' is but our fay'; whoever comes between us and it, we shall judge him with our swords. When he had prayed he commanded the man be brought and admitted to him, and seated him with him upon the couch. Then he permitted the people and they entered upon him. Then he said: O people, I spoke on the first Friday and no one answered me, and on the second and no one answered me. When the third came, this one revived me — may Allah revive him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will come a people who speak and are not answered; they will plunge into the Fire plunging like apes."" So I feared Allah would make me among them. When this one answered me, he revived me — may Allah revive him — and I hope Allah will not make me among them."
"7385","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from 'Umayr ibn Hani', from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan that he addressed them and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will ever remain of my nation a community upholding the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; neither those who forsake them nor those who oppose them will harm them, until the command of Allah comes while they are upon that."" 'Umayr said: Malik ibn Yukhamir al-Saksaki said: O Commander of the Believers, I heard Mu'adh ibn Jabal say: And they are in Sham. So Mu'awiyah said: This is Malik ibn Yukhamir — and he has the good trait — claiming he heard Mu'adh say: They are the people of Sham."
"7386","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: Mu'awiyah arrived and was brought a staff with a rag on its head. He said: I never thought anyone did this except the Jews; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of that and called it falsehood."
"7387","Repeated: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his uncle 'Isa ibn Talhah who said: I was sitting with Mu'awiyah when the mu'adhdhin came to announce the prayer to him. Mu'awiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection are the mu'adhdhins."""
"7388","'Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-'Ala' ibn Hilal al-Raqqi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu al-Fayd, from Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali al-Sulami who said: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan led us in Maghrib, three rak'ahs, then stood for two rak'ahs, so they glorified Allah to alert him, and he gestured to them to stand. When he finished his prayer and gave salam, he turned and addressed them, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as you saw me do; had I not seen him do it, I would not have done it."
"7389","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Maladh al-Ash'ari narrating, from Numayr ibn Aws, from Malik ibn Masruh, from 'Amir ibn Abi 'Amir al-Ash'ari, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Ash'aris: ""They are from me and I am from them."" He said: So I narrated it to Mu'awiyah, and he said: Not so; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — he only said: ""They are from me and to me."" He said: I said: Not so; my father narrated to me — he only said: ""They are from me and I am from them."" He said: Then you are more knowledgeable of your father's hadith."
"7390","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Marhum narrated to me, Abu al-Na'amah al-Sa'di narrated to us, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Mu'awiyah went out to a circle in the mosque and said: What has seated you? They said: We sat remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic. He said: By Allah, did nothing seat you but that? They said: By Allah, nothing seated us but that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to a circle of his companions and said: ""What has seated you?"" They said: We sat remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and praising Him for guiding us to Islam and bestowing it upon us. He said: ""By Allah, did nothing seat you but that?"" They said: By Allah, nothing seated us but that. He said: ""I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you, but Jibril came to me and informed me that Allah boasts of you to the angels."""
"7391","'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from 'Isa ibn Talhah, from Mu'awiyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The longest-necked of people on the Day of Resurrection are the mu'adhdhins."""
"7392","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl al-Rasi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Thawr, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When you pursue the faults of people, you corrupt them — or nearly corrupt them."" He said: Abu al-Darda' says: A word Mu'awiyah heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — Allah benefited him by it."
"7393","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq say: Nasr ibn al-Hajjaj ibn 'Ilat al-Sulami claimed 'Abdullah ibn Rabah, freedman of Khalid ibn al-Walid. So 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid stood and said: My freedman was born on my freedman's bed; and Nasr said: My brother entrusted me with his station. He said: Their dispute grew long, so they entered with him upon Mu'awiyah — with Fihr under his head — and both made their claim. Mu'awiyah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."" Nasr said: Then where is this judgment of yours, O Mu'awiyah, concerning Ziyad? Mu'awiyah said: The judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better than the judgment of Mu'awiyah. So 'Abdullah ibn Rabah would not concede to Nasr what he claimed. Nasr said: Rich..."
"7394","Hadith of Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""No cutter (of kinship) will enter Paradise."""
"7395","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father — and Jubayr had met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who said: ""No cutter (of kinship) will enter Paradise."""
"7396","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib with al-Tur."
"7397","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No cutter (of kinship) will enter Paradise."""
"7398","Abu Khaythamah and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim both narrated to us, they said: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom disbelief is effaced, and I am al-Hashir at whose heels people will be gathered, and I am al-'Aqib after whom there is no prophet."""
"7399","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Abdullah ibn Babah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""O Banu 'Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House and prays at any hour he wishes, of night or day."""
"7400","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: We discussed ghusl from janabah in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""As for me, I pour over my head three times."""
"7401","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Asim al-'Anazi, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the prayer he said: ""Allah is Most Great, Most Great; and praise be to Allah abundantly — three times — glory be to Allah morning and evening — three times — I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan: from his blowing, his prodding, and his poetry."" 'Amr said: His blowing is pride, his prodding is madness, and his poetry is poetry."
"7402","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the share of the near kin between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I came to him, I and 'Uthman, and said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Hashim — their merit is undeniable by your place among them which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave you. What of Banu al-Muttalib — you gave them and withheld from us, though we and they are to you of one standing? He said: ""They never separated from me in pre-Islamic times nor in Islam; Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one thing,"" and he interlaced his fingers."
"7403","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Awf, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Qurashi has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh."" It was said to al-Zuhri: What did he mean by it? He said: Soundness of judgment."
"7404","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey of his, and he said: ""The people of Yemen will come upon you as though they are clouds; they are the best of those on earth."" A man from the Ansar said: Except us, O Messenger of Allah? He fell silent. Then he repeated it, and he fell silent. Then he repeated it a third time: Except us, O Messenger of Allah? So he said — in a faint word — ""Except you."""
"7405","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for something, and he said to her: Come back to me. She said to him: O Messenger of Allah, if I return and do not find you — hinting at death — he said: ""If you do not find me, then meet Abu Bakr."""
"7406","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr Abu 'Amir narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which lands are the worst? He said: I do not know. When Jibril — peace be upon him — came to him, he said: O Jibril, which lands are the worst? He said: I do not know, until I ask my Lord, Mighty and Majestic. So Jibril went and remained as long as Allah willed, then came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me which lands are the worst, and I said I do not know; and I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, which lands are the worst, and He said: Their markets."
"7407","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle who said: 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that Muhammad ibn Jubayr said: Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me that while he was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the people with him — on his return from Hunayn — the Bedouins clung to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, until they forced him to a samurah tree and his cloak was snatched. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: ""Give me my cloak. Had the number of these thorn-trees been livestock, I would have divided it among you; then you would not find me miserly, nor lying, nor cowardly."""
"7408","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Nu'man ibn Salim who said: I heard a man who heard Jubayr say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, some people say: We have no rewards in Makkah? He said: ""Your rewards will surely come to you, even if you were in the burrow of a fox."""
"7409","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in pre-Islamic times, Islam only strengthened it."""
"7410","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim who said: I heard one of my brothers narrating, from my father, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the ransom of the polytheists, having not yet embraced Islam that day. He said: So I reached him while he was praying Maghrib, reciting in it al-Tur, as though my heart split when I heard the Qur'an."
"7411","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven every night and says: Is there any caller, that I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness, that I may forgive him?"""
"7412","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, the like of it."
"7413","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: And 'Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and said: Who will guard us tonight, not sleeping through the Fajr prayer? Bilal said: I will. Then he faced the rising of the sun, and their ears were struck, and nothing woke them but the heat of the sun. So they stood, hastened and performed ablution; Bilal gave the adhan, and they prayed the two rak'ahs, then prayed Fajr."
"7414","Zuhayr narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine exceeds other mosques by a thousand prayers — except the Sacred Mosque."""
"7415","Sulayman al-Shadhakuni narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque."""
"7416","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Muhammad ibn Muslim mentioned, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father Jubayr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say while addressing the people at al-Khayf: ""May Allah brighten a servant who hears my saying, memorizes it, then conveys it to one who did not hear it. For many a carrier of understanding has no understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of a believer never harbors deceit: sincerity of deed for Allah, obedience to those in authority, and adherence to the community — for their supplication encompasses those behind them."""
"7417","Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr narrated to us, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father: the like of the hadith of Ibn Shihab, adding nothing and omitting nothing."
"7418","Harun ibn Ma'ruf and Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Abdullah ibn Babah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im — raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — that he said: ""O Banu 'Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House or prays at any hour of night or day."""
"7419","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Had al-Mut'im been alive"" — he said: and he had a favor with him — ""and had spoken to me concerning these filthy ones, I would have released them"" — the captives of Badr."
"7420","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Surad say: I heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im say: Ghusl from janabah was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""As for me, I pour over my head three times."""
"7421","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim who said: One of my brothers informed me, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a ransom from the ransoms of the polytheists. He said: So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying Maghrib, and he recited in it al-Tur, as though my heart split when I heard the Qur'an."
"7422","Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hakam al-Qudaydi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Khalid al-Khuza'i, that Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Jubayr, would you love, when you go out on a journey, to be of the best of your companions in appearance and the most abundant in provision?"" I said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransomed for you. He said: ""Then recite these five surahs: {Say: O disbelievers}, and {When the help of Allah comes and the victory}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}, and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak}, and {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind}; and open each surah with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,' and end your recitation with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.'"" Jubayr said: I was wealthy, of much property, and I would go out with whomever Allah willed I go out with on a journey, being the shabbiest of them in appearance and the least in provision. Ever since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught them to me and I recited them, I am among the best of them in appearance and the most abundant in provision, until I return from that journey of mine."
"7423","Hadith of Abu Barzah al-Aslami from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la Abu Muhammad al-Sami narrated to us, Sa'id — meaning al-Jurayri — narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Mawalah al-Qushayri who said: I was in al-Ahwaz when an elderly corpulent shaykh passed by me upon a mule, saying: O Allah, my generation of this nation has gone; join me with them. So I caught up to him with my mount and said: And I, may Allah have mercy on you. He said: And this companion of mine, if he desires that. He said: Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best of my nation are my generation, then those who follow them"" — I do not know whether he mentioned the third or not — ""then there will succeed a people among whom obesity will appear, and they will pour forth testimony though not asked for it."" And behold, he was Abu Barzah al-Aslami."
"7424","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, their neighbor, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from 'Abdullah ibn Mutarrif, from Abu Barzah who said: The most hateful tribes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Banu Umayyah, Thaqif, and Banu Hanifah."
"7425","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Awf, from Sayyar ibn Salamah, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked sleep before 'Isha' and talk after it. He said: And he would recite in the morning prayer from sixty to a hundred verses, and each one of us would recognize the one next to him."
"7426","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jurayj, from Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O assembly of those who believe with their tongues while faith has not entered their hearts, do not backbite the Muslims, nor pursue their faults; for whoever pursues the faults of the Muslims, Allah will pursue his fault until He exposes him in his house."""
"7427","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jurayj, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — and he mentioned the like of it."
"7428","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us, from 'Awf who said: Abu al-Minhal narrated to me, he said: My father set out, and I set out with him, and we entered upon Abu Barzah al-Aslami. My father said to him: Narrate to us how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prescribed prayer. He said: He would pray al-hajir, which you call the first, when the sun declined; and pray 'Asr when one of us would return to his lodging at the farthest part of Madinah while the sun was still alive. He said: And I forgot what he said about Maghrib. He said: And he liked to delay 'Isha', which you call al-'atamah; and he disliked sleep before it and talk after it; and he would turn from the morning prayer when a man would recognize his companion; and he would recite from sixty to a hundred."
"7429","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Dinar, from Abu Hashim, from Abu al-'Aliyah, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to rise from a sitting, he would say: ""Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."""
"7430","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Aban ibn Sam'ah, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barzah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed I may benefit by. He said: ""Remove harm from the path of the Muslims."""
"7431","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Barzah, that a slave-girl, while upon a camel — or a riding beast — carrying the people's goods between two mountains, the mountain straitened her; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon her, and when she saw him she began saying: Hal! O Allah, curse him, O Allah, curse him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is the owner of the slave-girl? Let no riding beast or camel upon which is a curse from Allah accompany us"" — or as he said."
"7432","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the morning prayer from sixty to a hundred."
"7433","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Umm al-Aswad narrated to me, from Munyah, from the hadith of Abu Barzah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had nine wives. One day he said: ""The best of you is the longest-handed of you."" So each one stood placing her hand upon the wall. He said: I do not mean this; rather the most skillful of you with her hands."
"7434","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: 'Awf narrated to me, from Musawir ibn 'Ubayd who said: Abu Barzah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a man of ours called Ma'iz ibn Malik."
"7435","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu al-Wazi' narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Barzah narrating, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to some Arab tribes concerning something — I do not know what it was — and they reviled him, insulted him, and struck him. So he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: As for you, had you gone to the people of Oman, they would not have insulted you nor struck you."
"7436","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Umm al-Aswad, from Munyah, from the hadith of Abu Barzah who said: They asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about an uncircumcised man — may he perform Hajj to the House of Allah? He said: ""No; Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbade me that until he is circumcised."""
"7437","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jurayj, from Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The feet of the servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about his life — how he spent it; and about his knowledge — what he did with it; and about his wealth — from where he earned it and in what he spent it; and about his body — in what he wore it out."""
"7438","Hudbah narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu al-Wazi' Jabir ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to a tribe among the Arab tribes concerning something — I do not know what it was — and they insulted him and struck him. So he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of that to him. He said: ""But had my messenger gone to the people of Oman, they would not have insulted him nor struck him."""
"7439","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir and Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn 'Amr ibn al-Ahwas who said: Abu Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Barzah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when he heard two men singing, one saying to his companion. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is this?"" He said: So it was said to him: So-and-so and so-and-so. He said: So he said: ""O Allah, cast them headlong into tribulation and thrust them into the Fire thrusting."""
"7440","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn 'Amr ibn al-Ahwas who said: The master of this house, Abu Hilal, narrated to me that he heard Abu Barzah al-Aslami narrating that they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they heard singing and craned toward it. A man stood and listened — that was before wine was forbidden — then came to them and returned, saying: This is so-and-so and so-and-so, the two singing, each answering the other, and he says — and he mentioned the like of it."
"7441","Ahmad — meaning Ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi — narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Barzah, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Ghifar — may Allah forgive it; and Aslam — may Allah grant it peace. I did not say it; rather Allah said it."""
"7442","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Umm al-Aswad bint Yazid, freedwoman of Abu Barzah al-Aslami, narrated to us, she said: Munyah bint 'Ubayd ibn Abi Barzah narrated to me, from her grandfather Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever consoles the bereaved mother will be clothed with a cloak of Paradise."""
"7443","'Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Nafi' ibn al-Harith, from Abu Barzah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will raise on the Day of Resurrection a people from their graves with their mouths blazing with fire."" It was said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""Have you not seen that Allah says: {Indeed those who consume the wealth of orphans unjustly only consume fire in their bellies}?"""
"7444","And from Nafi' ibn al-Harith, Abu Barzah narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Indeed lying blackens the face, and tale-bearing is the punishment of the grave."""
"7445","And from Nafi', from Abu Barzah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""After me there will be rulers: if you obey them they will make you disbelieve, and if you disobey them they will kill you — rulers of disbelief and heads of misguidance."""
"7446","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us — from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn 'Amr ibn al-Ahwas al-Azdi who said: Abu Hilal, master of this house, narrated to me, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands in supplication until the whiteness of his armpits was seen."
"7447","Hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering the sermon standing, then sitting without speaking, then standing and delivering another sermon upon his pulpit. Whoever narrates to you that he saw him delivering the sermon sitting, do not believe him."
"7448","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Before the Hour there will be liars."""
"7449","Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""I am your forerunner at the Hawd, and the distance between its two ends is as between San'a' and Aylah; as though the pitchers in it are the stars."""
"7450","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A band of Muslims — or of believers — will surely conquer the treasure of the family of Kisra which is in the white (palace)."" He said: And I heard him say: ""Allah named Madinah Tabah."""
"7451","And with his isnad, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: A mule died belonging to a man, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling. Jabir claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to its owner: ""What have you that spares you from it?"" He said: Nothing. He said: ""Go and eat it."""
"7452","And from Jabir who said: I saw Ma'iz ibn Malik when he was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bareheaded, wearing no cloak. He testified against himself four times that he had committed adultery. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Perhaps...?"" He said: No, by Allah, the other one has indeed committed adultery. He said: So he stoned him. Then he addressed and said: ""Whenever they go forth in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind with a bleating like the bleating of the billy-goat, granting one of them the heap (of food). If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, enables me over any of them, I shall surely make an example of him for them."""
"7453","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed like your prayer, and would delay al-'atamah a little after your prayer, and would lighten the prayer."
"7454","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: A she-camel belonging to some people of Banu Sulaym or others of the tribe died, and they were a needy household. So they asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about eating it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them to eat it, and it sufficed them their winter."
"7455","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times, and his companions would recite poetry to one another and recall something of the affairs of pre-Islamic times, and perhaps he would smile along with them."
"7456","And from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: Bilal would call the adhan for Zuhr when the sun declined, and he would sometimes delay the iqamah, but would not delay the adhan beyond its time."
"7457","And from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"7458","And from Jabir who said: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than a hundred times, and he never addressed except standing, and he would sit a sitting."
"7459","And from Jabir who said: When we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each of us would sit where he reached."
"7460","And from Jabir who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a day of Eid, and he neither gave adhan nor iqamah."
"7461","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had slender shanks; when you saw him you would say: Kohl-eyed — though he was not kohl-eyed — and he laughed only smiling."
"7462","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, that he heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: The front of the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had turned grey; when he oiled and combed it, it did not show, but when disheveled you would see it. He had abundant beard hair. A man said: Was his face like the sword? He said: No — like the sun and the moon, round. He said: And I saw his seal by his shoulder, like the egg of the ostrich, resembling his body."
"7463","'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him reclining upon his elbow."
"7464","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn al-'Awwam narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: In the two shanks of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was slenderness; he laughed only smiling; and when you looked at him you would say: Kohl-eyed, though he was not kohl-eyed."
"7465","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He would recite in Fajr {Qaf, and the Glorious Qur'an}, and his prayer thereafter was light."
"7466","Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I pray in the garment in which I go to my wife? He said: Yes, unless you see something in it, then wash it."
"7467","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""I am the forerunner at the Hawd."""
"7468","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Three things I fear for my nation: seeking rain by the stars, tyranny of the ruler, and denial of the decree."""
"7469","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Muhajir ibn Mismar, from 'Amir ibn Sa'd who said: I wrote to Jabir ibn Samurah, with my servant Nafi': Inform me of something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he wrote: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday, on the evening of the stoning of al-Aslami, say: ""The religion will ever remain standing until the Hour comes, and there will be over you twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."" And I heard him say: ""A band of Muslims will conquer the white house — the house of Kisra and the family of Kisra."""
"7470","And I heard him say: ""Before the Hour there will be liars, so beware of them."""
"7471","And I heard him say: When Allah gives one of you good, let him begin with himself and the people of his household."
"7472","And I heard him say: I am your forerunner at the Basin."
"7473","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Siyah, from Imran ibn Riyah, from Ali ibn Umarah, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I was in a gathering in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was present, and my father Samurah was sitting in front of me, and he said: Obscenity and indecent speech are in no way part of Islam, and among the people with the best Islam are those with the best character."
"7474","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Muadh narrated to me, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Makkah there is a stone that used to greet me on the nights I was sent, and I recognize it whenever I pass by it."
"7475","Amir ibn Abdullah ibn Barrad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwai - of Qays - who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Three things I fear for my ummah: seeking rain by the stars, the tyranny of the ruler, and denial of the Decree."
"7476","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."
"7477","Ishaq narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Tamim al-Tai, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw people raising their hands, and he said: What is with them raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still in prayer."
"7478","And from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw people praying with their heads raised to the sky, and he said: Men who stare with their eyes toward the sky shall stop, or their sight shall not return to them."
"7479","And from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and said: Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do they line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the first rows and press together in the row. He said: And he went out to the mosque while they were in separate circles in the mosque, and he said: Why do I see you in scattered groups?"
"7480","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I saw the Seal of Prophethood between the shoulders of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as if it were a dove's egg."
"7481","Ishaq narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Simak who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Before the Hour there will be liars. Simak said: My father said to me: So beware of them."
"7482","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, reporting from Abu Ishaq, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a moonlit night wearing a red garment, and I kept looking at him and at the moon, and he was in my eyes more beautiful than the moon."
"7483","Abu Hammam narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am your forerunner at the Basin, and the distance between its two ends is as between Sanaa and Aylah, as if its pitchers were like stars."
"7484","Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi Abu Wahb narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I pray in the garment in which I go to my wife? He said: Yes, unless you see something in it, then wash it."
"7485","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Sulayman who said: Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi narrated to me, from Tamim ibn Tarafah al-Tai, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while they had raised their hands, and he said: They have raised their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses; be still in prayer."
"7486","And from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not line up as the angels who are before their Lord line up? He said: How are the angels who are before their Lord? He said: They complete the first rows and press together in the row."
"7487","And from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out while they were in circles in the mosque, and he said: Why do I see you in scattered groups?"
"7488","The hadith of Wathilah ibn al-Asqa. Said ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Samman narrated to us, Anbasah narrated to us, Hammad the freedman of Umayyah narrated to us, from Janah the freedman of al-Walid, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your youth is he who resembles your elders, and the worst of your elders is he who resembles your youth."
"7489","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, al-Gharif ibn Ayyash ibn Fayruz al-Daylami narrated to us, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: Some people of Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: A companion of ours has incurred doom. He said: Then let him free a slave; Allah will free, for each of its limbs, a limb of him from the Fire."
"7490","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai, from Abu Ammar, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah chose Kinanah from the children of Ismail, and chose Quraysh from Kinanah, and chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."
"7491","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Abu Ammar Shaddad, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated Ali on his right and Fatimah on his left, and Hasan and Husayn before him, and covered them with a garment, and said: O Allah, these are the people of my household, and the people of my household come to You, not to the Fire."
"7492","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Abu Ammar, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah chose Banu Kinanah from Banu Ismail, and chose Quraysh from Banu Kinanah, and chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."
"7493","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tustari narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awzai who said: Rabiah narrated to me, he said: I heard Wathilah ibn al-Asqa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: You claim that I am the last of you to die; rather I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in scattered bands, some of you destroying others."
"7494","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Shami, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Count the verses in the voluntary prayer, and do not count them in the obligatory prayer."
"7495","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Rabiah, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: You claim that I am the last of you to die; rather I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in scattered bands, some of you striking the necks of others."
"7496","Abu Hammam narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Qurashi who said: Anbasah ibn Said al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Makhul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intimate acts of women with one another is adultery."
"7497","Abu al-Ashath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Ubayd ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Thalabah narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa who said: I approached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the mosque of al-Khayf, and his Companions said to me: Away from here, O Wathilah, meaning step away from the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for he has only come to ask. He said: So I drew near and said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about a matter we will take from you after you. He said: Your own self will give you the ruling. He said: I said: How can I attain that? He said: Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, even if those who give rulings give you rulings. I said: How can I know that? He said: Place your hand upon your heart, for the heart is at rest with the lawful and is not at rest with the unlawful, and the Godfearing Muslim leaves the small thing fearing to fall into the great thing. I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, what is partisanship? He said: He who aids his people upon wrongdoing. I said: Who is the greedy one? He said: He who seeks gain from other than its lawful source. I said: Who is the Godfearing one? He said: He who stops at the doubtful matter. I said: Who is the believer? He said: He whom people trust with their wealth and their blood. I said: Who is the Muslim? He said: He from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. I said: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of wisdom before an unjust ruler."
"7498","The hadith of Abdullah ibn Salam. Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman al-Kilabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Mamar ibn Rashid, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub, from Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; and the first for whom the earth will split, and the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted; in my hand is the banner of praise, beneath me Adam and those below him."
"7499","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Hakam al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Ala al-Madini narrated to me, he who is called al-Razi, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a piece of barley bread, then take a date and place it upon it, then say: This is the condiment of this."
"7500","Abu Yasir Ammar narrated to us, Hisham Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"7501","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid dinars in advance to a Jewish man for specified dates to a specified term, so the Jew said: From the dates of the garden of Banu Fulan? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for from the dates of the garden of Banu Fulan, then no."
"7502","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai who said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, he said: Hilal narrated to me that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Salam narrated to him, or he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: We discussed among ourselves and said: Which of you will go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic? And we were reluctant for any of us to stand, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for us man by man until he gathered us, and we came pointing to one another, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us the surah: Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise. O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do. He recited them from its beginning to its end. He said: So Abdullah ibn Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end. He said: So Ata recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: So Hilal recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awzai said: So Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end."
"7503","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from the nephew of Abdullah ibn Salam, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: My name in the pre-Islamic age was so-and-so; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named me Abdullah."
"7504","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Salam who said: We mentioned the deeds most beloved to Allah and said: Who will ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for us? And we were reluctant to ask him, so he singled us out man by man until we gathered before him, some of us moving toward others, and we did not know; then he sent for us, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us this surah: Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, up to His saying: A compact structure. Ibn Salam said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us the whole surah from its beginning to its end. Abu Salamah said: And Abdullah ibn Salam recited to us the surah from its beginning to its end."
"7505","Ammar Abu Yasir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ziyad Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning."
"7506","Abu Yasir Ammar narrated to us, Abu al-Miqdam Hisham ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is part of faith."
"7507","The hadith of Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali. Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Jabir, from Amir, from Jarir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishment of prayer, giving of zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting of Ramadan."
"7508","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Said, from Abu Zurah ibn Amr ibn Jarir who said: Jarir said: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, and to be sincere to every Muslim. He said: So when he bought something - it being dearer to me than its price - he would say to its owner: By Allah, what we take from you is dearer to us than what we give you. He said: Intending fulfillment of that pledge."
"7509","Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fasting three days of every month is fasting the lifetime: the white days, the morning of the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."
"7510","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to me, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment he would say: In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the creed of the Messenger of Allah: Do not steal from the spoils, nor betray, nor mutilate, nor kill children."
"7511","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Shuabah, from Jabir, from Tariq al-Tamimi, from Jarir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some women and greeted them."
"7512","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Dawud al-Araj narrated to us, from al-Shaabi, from Jarir ibn Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah, establishment of prayer, giving of zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting of Ramadan."
"7513","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ubaydullah ibn Jarir al-Bajali, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There are no people among whom is a man committing sins - they being stronger and mightier than him - and they do not change him, except that Allah strikes them with His punishment."
"7514","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah who said: I heard Jarir ibn Abdullah - when al-Mughirah ibn Shuabah died and another was appointed, and I saw Jarir delivering a sermon - say: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah alone with no partner for Him, and that you hear and obey until an amir comes to you. He said: Then he mentioned al-Mughirah and said: Seek forgiveness for him; may Allah pardon him, for he loved well-being. Then he said: To proceed, I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me sincerity to every Muslim; so by the Lord of this mosque, I am indeed sincere to you."
"7515","The hadith of Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ishaq ibn Abi Israil and Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard it from Sahl ibn Sad who said: A man peeped through a hole into the chamber of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had an iron comb with which he was scratching his head, and he said: Had I known you were looking, I would have poked it into your eye; seeking permission was only made on account of sight."
"7516","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain well so long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."
"7517","And from Sahl ibn Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand, or seven hundred thousand, of my ummah will enter Paradise, holding to one another, or: grasping one another - Abu Hazim said: I do not know which - with one another."
"7518","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, who heard Sahl ibn Sad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is beset by something in his prayer, then clapping is for women and glorifying Allah is for men."
"7519","I heard Ishaq say: I heard Sufyan say: Abu Hazim used to say: I heard Sahl ibn Sad say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The place of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."
"7520","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were carrying dust upon our heads, and he said: O Allah, there is no life but the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"7521","Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uhud is a pillar among the pillars of Paradise."
"7522","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, who heard it from Sahl ibn Sad, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Words broke out between al-Aws and al-Khazraj until some of them assailed others, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and informed, and he went to them; then Bilal called the adhan for prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delayed, and when he was delayed the iqamah for prayer was called, and Abu Bakr stepped forward leading the people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from that coming of his and passed through the people until he reached the row next to Abu Bakr, and the people clapped; and Abu Bakr would not turn in prayer, but when he heard the clapping he turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to remain firm. He said: Allah would not let the son of Abu Quhafah be seen before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said to the people: What is with you that when something befalls you in your prayer you clap? That is only for women; whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him say: Glory be to Allah."
"7523","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that Uhud shook while upon it were the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be still, Uhud, for upon you is none but a Prophet, or a truthful one, or two martyrs."
"7524","Ishaq narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, from his father who said: We visited Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi among some women, and he said: Had I given you drink from the well of Budaah you would dislike that, yet by Allah I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink from its water."
"7525","Ishaq narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sad, who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned Paradise - say: In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"7526","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: I heard him narrate that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and offered herself to him, and he remained silent; then she offered herself to him, and he remained silent. I saw her standing a long while - or he said: a while - offering herself to him while he was silent. Then a man stood - I think he said: from the Ansar - and said: If you have no need of her, then marry her to me. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then go and seek something, even an iron ring. So he went and returned, and said: By Allah, I found nothing except this garment of mine; I will split it between me and her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no surplus in your garment beyond your need."
"7527","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, who heard Sahl ibn Sad say concerning the people: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman stood and said: She has offered herself to him, so give your opinion concerning her. Then a man of the people stood and said: Marry her to me, but he did not reply to him. Then she said: She has offered herself to you. Then a man stood and said: Marry her to me. Then he stood a third time and said: Do you have anything? He said: No. He said: Then go and seek. He said: So he went and sought, and said: I found nothing. He said: Then go and seek, even an iron ring. He said: So he went and returned, and said: I found nothing. He said: Do you have anything of the Quran with you? He said: Yes, such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah. So he said: Go, for I have married her to you for what you have of the Quran."
"7528","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent, and the Hour, like this from this - and Sufyan described with his index finger, pointing with it."
"7529","Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: There was fighting between Banu Amr ibn Awf, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to them to make peace between them, having already prayed Zuhr, and he said to Bilal: If the Asr prayer comes and I have not come, then command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. When the Asr prayer came, Bilal called the adhan and the iqamah and said: O Abu Bakr, step forward. So Abu Bakr stepped forward. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, parting the rows, and when the people saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they clapped, meaning applause. He said: And Abu Bakr, when he entered prayer, would not turn; but when he saw the clapping would not stop, he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him to continue. Abu Bakr tarried a moment praising Allah for the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Continue. Then Abu Bakr walked backward, meaning upon his heels. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he stepped forward and led the people in their prayer. When he finished his prayer he said: O Abu Bakr, what prevented you, when I gestured to you, from continuing? Abu Bakr said: It was not for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer. Then he said to the people: When something befalls you in your prayer, let the men glorify Allah and the women clap."
"7530","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Zammani narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Amr. [The report breaks off here with no further text.]"
"7531","And from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Below Allah are seventy thousand veils of light and darkness, and no soul hears anything of the sound of those veils but its soul departs."
"7532","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Muhammad al-Madini narrate, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: With Allah are treasuries of good and evil, whose keys are men; so blessed is he whom He makes a key to good and a lock to evil, and woe to he whom He makes a lock to good and a key to evil."
"7533","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on the day of Khaybar: I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man by whose hand Allah will grant victory. So the people spent the night discussing which of them would be given it. When morning came, the people went early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), all of them hoping to be given it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is Ali ibn Abi Talib? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he is complaining of his eyes. So he ordered him brought and he was called; then he spat in his eyes and supplicated for him, and he was healed on the spot, as if nothing had been wrong with him. Then he handed the banner to him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we fight them? He said: Gently; proceed until you halt in their courtyard, then call them to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to His Messenger, until they become like us, and inform them of what is due upon them therein of the truth. By Allah, for Allah to guide through your guidance a single man is better for you than red camels."
"7534","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see a chamber among the chambers of Paradise as you see the brilliant star on the eastern or western horizon."
"7535","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For those who fast there is a gate in Paradise called al-Rayyan; none but them shall enter through it. When the last of them enters it is closed; whoever enters through it drinks, and whoever drinks shall never thirst again."
"7536","And from Sahl ibn Sad that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while mentioning Paradise, say: In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has not occurred to the heart of a human."
"7537","And from Sahl ibn Sad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going forth or an evening going forth, meaning in the path of Allah, is better than the world and what is in it."
"7538","Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qudamah ibn Ibrahim who said: I saw al-Hajjaj beating Abbas ibn Sahl concerning the affair of Ibn al-Zubayr, so Sahl ibn Sad came to him, an old man with two braids wearing two garments, a waist-wrapper and a cloak, and stood between the two rows and said: O Hajjaj, will you not observe concerning us the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bequeath concerning you? He said: He bequeathed that good be done to the doers of good among the Ansar and that their wrongdoers be pardoned. He said: So he released him."
"7539","Musab narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: I used to take the predawn meal with my family, then hasten so as to catch the prostration with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7540","Dawud ibn Amr ibn Zuhayr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Zuhrah ibn Amr ibn Mabad al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The length of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it, and a morning going forth in the path of Allah or an evening going forth is better than the world and what is in it."
"7541","And from Abu Hazim who said: Sahl ibn Sad informed me, he said: I witnessed three things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when his incisor tooth was broken, his face was wounded, and the helmet was crushed upon his head; and I know who washed the blood from his face, and who poured water upon him, and what was applied to stop it. [The narration breaks off at Abu Yala.]"
"7542","Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjumani Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abi Hazim, narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sad, that a man asked him: Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wounded? He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded, his incisor tooth was broken, and the helmet was crushed upon his head. Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wash the blood, and Ali would pour water upon her with the shield. When Fatimah saw that the water only increased the blood, Fatimah took a piece of mat and burnt it, until when it became ashes she stuck it to the wound, and the blood stopped."
"7543","And from Sahl ibn Sad that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man by whose hand Allah will grant victory. He said: So the people spent the night discussing that and considering which of them would be given it. When morning came, the people went early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), all hoping to be given it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is Ali ibn Abi Talib? They said: O Messenger of Allah, he is complaining of his eyes. So he ordered him brought and he was called; then he spat in his eyes and supplicated for him, and he was healed on the spot, as if nothing had been wrong with him. Then he gave him the banner, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we fight them until they become like us? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently; when you halt in their courtyard, call them to Islam and inform them of what is due upon them therein of the truth. By Allah, for Allah to guide through your guidance a single man is better for you than red camels."
"7544","And from Sahl ibn Sad who said: Between the prayer place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the wall was the passage of a sheep."
"7545","And from Sahl ibn Sad who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to offer myself to you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at her, raising his gaze upon her and lowering it. When her standing grew long she stepped aside and sat. Then a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you have no need of her, then marry her to me. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then go. So he went and returned, and said: I found nothing. He said: Go and look, even an iron ring. He said: So he went and returned, and said: O Messenger of Allah, no, not even an iron ring; this is my waist-wrapper, and he has no cloak; I will give it to her as dowry. So he said: Your waist-wrapper, if she wears it there will be nothing of it upon you, and if you wear it there will be nothing of it upon her. He said: When his sitting grew long he stood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him turning away, so he ordered him brought and he was called. He said: What do you have of the Quran? He said: I have such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah among the surahs; he enumerated them. So he said: Go, for I have given her to you in marriage for what you have of the Quran."
"7546","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, Sahl ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: When this verse was revealed: Eat and drink until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread, a man would take the white thread and the black thread and eat until he could distinguish them, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Of the dawn. So that clarified it."
"7547","Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said - Bishr said: And I heard it from Abu Hazim - that some Muslim men would attend prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with their garments tied upon their necks, none of them having but a single garment."
"7548","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: Women were commanded in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer not to raise their heads until the men took their seats upon the ground, because of the unsightliness of the garments. Bishr said: I heard it from Abu Hazim."
"7549","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one uttering the talbiyah utters it but the ground that follows him on this side and that, on his right and on his left, utters it too, until the dust ends."
"7550","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman the judge narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, on the day of Uhud we saw nothing like what so-and-so did; a man came to him! The people fled but he did not flee, and he left none of the polytheists scattered or isolated but he pursued it striking it with his sword. He said: Who is he? He said: So his lineage was attributed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he did not recognize him; then he was described to him by his description but he did not recognize him, until the man appeared in person and he said: This, O Messenger of Allah, is the one we told you of. He said: This one? They said: Yes. He said: He is among the people of the Fire? He said: That weighed heavily upon the Muslims. They said: Which of us is among the people of Paradise if so-and-so is among the people of the Fire? So a man among the people said: O people, watch me; by Him in whose hand is my soul, he will not die upon the like of what he began the day upon, and I shall surely be his companion apart from you. Then he set out earnestly the next day, and the man would charge when he charged and return when he returned, watching what his affair would come to, until he was struck by a wound that pained him severely, so he hastened death: he placed the hilt of his sword upon the ground, then placed its point between his breasts, then bore down upon his sword until it came out from his back. And the man came running, saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah, until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And what is that? He said: O Messenger of Allah, the man who was mentioned to you, about whom you said he is among the people of the Fire - that weighed heavily upon the Muslims, and they said: Which of us is among the people of Paradise if so-and-so is among the people of the Fire? So I said: O people, watch me; by Him in whose hand is my soul, he will not die upon the like of what he began the day upon, and I shall surely be his companion apart from you. So I charged when he charged and returned when he returned, watching what his affair would come to, until he was struck by a wound that pained him severely, so he hastened death: he placed the hilt of his sword upon the ground and placed its point between his breasts, then bore down upon his sword until it came out from his back. There he is, O Messenger of Allah, writhing among his death-rattle. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may do the deeds of the people of Paradise as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of the Fire; and a man may do the deeds of the people of the Fire as it appears to people, yet he is among the people of Paradise."
"7551","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that Banu Amr ibn Awf had a dispute among them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to some of his Companions: Come with us to make peace between them. So he went out with some of his Companions; then prayer came, so Bilal stood and called the adhan, then drew near to Abu Bakr and said: Shall I call the iqamah so you lead the people in prayer while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is detained? He said: Yes. So he called the iqamah, and Abu Bakr stepped forward and prorclaimed the takbir over the people. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appeared from the rear of the mosque, moving through the rows, heading toward the qiblah, and when the Muslims saw him they clapped at Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded until he reached the first row, and when they clapped much Abu Bakr turned, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he stepped back, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned him to the qiblah, raised his hands and praised Allah, then stepped back with a withdrawal that was not belied until he entered the row. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and led the people in prayer until he finished his prayer. Then he turned to the people and said: O people, whoever is beset by something in his prayer, let him say: Glory be to Allah, for glorifying is for men and clapping is for women, meaning applause. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and said: What prevented you from remaining firm when I commanded you? He said: It was not fitting for the son of Abu Quhafah to lead the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer."
"7552","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Ayyash al-Hadrami who said: Yahya ibn Maymun the judge of Egypt informed me, he said: Sahl ibn Sad narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever awaits prayer is in prayer so long as he does not commit hadath."
"7553","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai who said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will console one another after me with consolation for me. So the people would say: What is this? And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, we met one another consoling one another for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7554","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Abu Hafs al-Taifi, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts the day of Arafah, he is forgiven two consecutive years."
"7555","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir who said: Abu Hazim narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection upon a white, dust-colored land like a loaf of pure bread, in which there is no landmark for anyone."
"7556","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: And Ayyash ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami narrated to me that Yahya ibn Maymun al-Hadrami narrated to him, he said: Sahl ibn Sad al-Ansari passed by me while I was sitting in the mosque by the enclosure, and said to me: Shall I not inform you of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So I said to a man beside me, between whom and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was none but this man: Yes, may Allah guide you aright, so inform me. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is in the mosque awaiting prayer is in prayer so long as prayer detains him."
"7557","Al-Qawariri narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhubab, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands supplicating upon a minbar or upon other than it; rather I saw him say like this - and Abu Said said: With the index finger of his right hand, and he curved it."
"7558","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, he said: My father said, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will remain well so long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."
"7559","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I and the guardian of the orphan are in Paradise, and he pointed with the index and the middle fingers."
"7560","Al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Said al-Madani narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything has a hump, and the hump of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah; whoever recites it in his house at night, Satan shall not enter his house for three nights, and whoever recites it by day, Satan shall not enter his house for three days."
"7561","Al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guarantees me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I shall guarantee him Paradise? The last of what was with Abu Amr ibn Hamdan al-Hiri of the Musnad of Abu Yala al-Mawsili, may Allah have mercy upon them both; and praise be to Allah as He deserves to be praised, and His blessings and peace upon the best of His creation and the manifester of His truth, Muhammad, and upon his family and his Companions."
